# Memex vLLM env file — read by the systemd unit at
# ~/.config/systemd/user/memex-vllm.service.
#
# All values shown commented are the *defaults* baked into
# scripts/serve-vllm.sh. Uncomment + edit a line to override.
#
# NOTE (ADR-0015, 2026-06-01): when the daemon launches vLLM it EXPORTS
# MEMEX_VLLM_{MODEL,QUANTIZATION,KV_CACHE_DTYPE} from the app config
# (`daemon/supervisor.orchestrator_serve_env`), so the orchestrator id is
# normally driven by `models.orchestrator` (MEMEX_MODELS__ORCHESTRATOR),
# NOT by hand-editing this file. These lines matter when you run
# serve-vllm.sh standalone (e.g. the bare systemd unit without the daemon).

# ── Model + binding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default orchestrator (12 GB tier): cyankiwi/Qwen3.5-4B-AWQ-4bit.
# Kill-switch (legacy): Qwen/Qwen3-8B-AWQ.
# MEMEX_VLLM_MODEL=cyankiwi/Qwen3.5-4B-AWQ-4bit
# MEMEX_VLLM_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MEMEX_VLLM_PORT=8000

# ── Quantization + context ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The 4B is compressed-tensors → NO --quantization flag (empty string).
# The 8B kill-switch uses awq_marlin. serve-vllm.sh derives the right
# value per model; set explicitly only when running standalone.
# MEMEX_VLLM_QUANTIZATION=          # empty for the 4B (compressed-tensors); awq_marlin for the 8B
# MEMEX_VLLM_KV_CACHE_DTYPE=auto    # 4B is an fp8 checkpoint → auto (fp16 KV); 8B uses fp8_e5m2
# MEMEX_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192     # 4B window; 8B kill-switch uses 6144

# ── GPU memory ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 0.62 = empirical 12 GB-rig setting for the Qwen3.5-4B (auto KV) + the
# in-process embedder + CPU/GPU reranker (peaked ~8.0 GB, ~4 GB slack).
# The 8B kill-switch uses 0.72. serve-vllm.sh keys this off the model id;
# bump to 0.80 on a 16 GB+ card for KV-cache headroom.
# MEMEX_VLLM_GPU_FRACTION=0.62

# ── Device pinning ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0

# ── Compilation knob ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment to disable CUDA-graph compilation (slower decode but
# faster startup, useful while debugging).
# MEMEX_VLLM_EAGER=1
